<title>USA: Jacor to buy four Kentucky radio stations.</title>
<headline>Jacor to buy four Kentucky radio stations.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacor Communications Inc said it agreed to buy four radio stations in Kentucky from entities controlled by Jim Champlin.</p>
<p>The company did not diclose terms of the transaction and officials there were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>The stations are WLKT-FM in Lexington; WLRS-FM in Louisville; and WMCC-FM and WLOC-AM in Munfordville.</p>
<p>The company now owns, operates or provides programming for 118 radio stations, it said, adding that the transaction is subject to regulatory approval.</p>
